# Transformation_NLLP publication: tracked, except the artifacts below.
# Build artifacts (.venv/ and __pycache__/ are already covered repo-wide).
publications/Transformation_NLLP/.quarto/
publications/Transformation_NLLP/manuscript_files/
publications/Transformation_NLLP/manuscript_executed_files/
publications/Transformation_NLLP/manuscript.tex
publications/Transformation_NLLP/manuscript.fdb_latexmk
# Internal decision log + study protocol, not audience-facing.
publications/Transformation_NLLP/DESIGN.md
# Regenerable ops output from scripts/ops/: blind-coded rubric renderings for
# the manual audit.
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/interim/audit/exam_*.md
# Run outputs from the judge/probe/audit dispatches — 23 MB of per-cell score
# rows. Regenerable from the platform, and git is not a data store; they ship
# with the dataset release. Every manuscript.qmd load goes through
# load_optional(), so the paper still renders from the tracked data alone;
# `make analyze` is what needs these back.
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/**/*.jsonl

# The repo-wide `*.json` rule above hides every JSON in the project. This
# publication's derived statistics are what the manuscript loads, so unignore
# them - then re-block the sensitive and heavy files, because for git the
# LAST matching pattern wins.
!publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/**/*.json
# Plaintext what-a-benger.net account passwords for the audit + probe
# fixtures. No analysis script reads them; setup_audit_project.py takes
# credentials as CLI args.
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/interim/audit/audit_users.json
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/interim/probes/probe_users.json
# Full Sachverhalt + Musterloesung for all 15 exams - corpus text we do not
# hold redistribution rights for. Same call as the Benchmark_EMNLP ZJS source
# trees below: ships via HF + Zenodo at release time, never via git.
# exams.json is the extract_exam_pack.py output; manuscript.qmd reads it via
# load_optional() and falls back to n_exams = 15, so the paper still renders.
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/interim/exams.json
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/interim/audit/audit_import.json
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/interim/audit/audit_import.resolved.json
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/interim/probes/probe_texts.json
# The blind-code -> rubric_id/generator_model_id key for the human audit.
# Same category as Benchmark_EMNLP's .grader_map.json: publishing it alongside the
# blind-coded audit sheet would undo the blinding. The de-blinded result the
# paper reports lives in data/processed/audit_stats.json, which carries no
# blind codes and is tracked.
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/interim/audit/KEY.json
# Dated eval-config backups from the dispatch runs — regenerable ops output.
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/interim/clone_eval_config_backup_*.json
# The 193 generated rubrics (21 MB) and the judge rows derived from them.
# Their `criteria` enumerate the expected solution steps of each exam, so they
# are a close derivative of the Musterloesungen — same redistribution call as
# the corpus text above. Ships via HF + Zenodo with the dataset release.
# Directory-level ignore: nothing under raw/ is publishable, and an excluded
# directory cannot be re-included by the `!...*.json` rule above.
publications/Transformation_NLLP/data/raw/

# Benchmark_EMNLP publication: tracked, except large/private artifacts.
# - raw subtrees hold 5 GB of platform exports + ZJS PDFs/source — ship via HF + Zenodo, not git
# - .grader_map.json is the private grader-anonymization key — never commit
# - ZJS variant trees (source_strict/, source_optimistic/) stay local until
#   legal picks one for release; only the chosen variant ships, via HF + Zenodo
#
# Note: blanket-ignoring `data/raw/` is wrong here — once a directory is
# ignored, files inside cannot be re-included via `!file/path`. So instead
# we ignore the specific heavy subtrees and the IP-clearance map files stay
# tracked by default.
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/zjs/source/
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/zjs/source_strict/
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/zjs/source_optimistic/
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/zjs/ZJS Fälle-tasks-*.json
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/zjs/zjs_merged*.json
# IP-clearance roster CSV carries the outreach email column (396 work emails).
# It is the input that produces ip_clearance.json (public, email-free); the
# CSV itself never ships. The roster is regenerated on demand from the
# upstream tracking sheet, not from this file.
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/zjs/ip_clearance_*.csv
# Scripts that hold real grader identities (name → uuid → email) for the
# one-shot anonymization + sample-building pipeline. Outputs are tracked and
# fully anonymized; the scripts themselves stay local until refactored to
# load identities from an external private file.
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/scripts/anonymize_graders.py
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/scripts/build_human_grading_sample.py
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/benchathon/
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/grundprinzipien/
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/mock/
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/archive/
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/.grader_map.json
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/.quarto/
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/manuscript_files/
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/manuscript.tex
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/manuscript.fdb_latexmk
# arXiv upload bundles are built locally via `make arxiv` and shipped to
# arXiv directly - never committed (the repo tree IS the source).
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/benger_arxiv_source*

# The repo-wide `*.json` rule below hides every JSON in the project. The
# Benchmark_EMNLP publication needs its small derived JSONs tracked (the ones
# the manuscript loads), so unignore them explicitly.
# Note: the IP-clearance roster (CSV with emails AND its email-free JSON
# derivative) stays out of the public repo — it's internal accounting and
# the redaction state is already encoded in source_strict/.
!publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/interim/*.json
!publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/processed/*.json
# The Qwen Thinking-vs-Instruct ablation sidecar (Appendix P input) is small
# and shippable. It was force-added under the old folder name; make the
# un-ignore explicit so a rename can never silently drop it again.
!publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/raw/ablation/*.json
# …but re-block all merged ZJS dumps. The unredacted `zjs.json` is the
# full-text 21 MB merge (never publish); the strict and optimistic variants
# are computed from raw/, ship only to HF/Zenodo at release time, and are
# regenerable from `scripts/zjs_apply_ip_clearance.py`. Keeping them out of
# git defers the strict-vs-optimistic legal choice to release time.
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/interim/zjs.json
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/interim/zjs_strict.json
publications/Benchmark_EMNLP/data/interim/zjs_optimistic.json

# LEXam_DE publication: tracked, except build artifacts and the result
# dumps below. The dumps ship as a Zenodo dataset instead; regenerate via
# publications/LEXam_DE/analysis/dump_results.sh (needs prod access).
publications/LEXam_DE/.quarto/
publications/LEXam_DE/manuscript_files/
publications/LEXam_DE/manuscript.tex
publications/LEXam_DE/manuscript.log
publications/LEXam_DE/manuscript.fdb_latexmk
publications/LEXam_DE/analysis/data/
# ...but the generated eval-config payloads are part of the rerun recipe
# (see LEXam_DE/README.md) and must survive the generic *.json rule.
!publications/LEXam_DE/configs/generated/*.json

# WIP publications - not yet ready for the public repo
publications/Watermark_Study/
